  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to the commencement of development, a Construction Method Statement shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The statement shall detail the measures to be implemented to mitigate and control noise, dust, vibration, and other environmental impacts arising from the construction works.\r\rReason: To comply with Policies 29 and 34 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "All Non-Road Mobile Machinery (NRMM) with a net power output of between 37kW and 560kW deployed on site during demolition, site clearance, and construction phases shall adhere to the emission standards outlined in Chapter 7 of the GLA Supplementary Planning Guidance \"Control of Dust and Emissions During Construction and Demolition\" (July 2014) or subsequent updates. No non-compliant machinery shall be present on site without prior written consent from the Local Planning Authority, and an up-to-date register of all on-site machinery must be maintained via the GLA NRMM web register.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 34 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and Policy SI 1 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "Prior to the commencement of development, a revised Energy Statement shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. This submission must incorporate 'as-designed' Standard Assessment Procedure (SAP) 10.2 worksheets confirming that the dwelling will achieve a minimum 35% reduction in regulated carbon dioxide (CO2) emissions compared against the Part L 2021 baseline. The submission must also include full technical specifications, layout plans, and rated generating capacities for the air source heat pump (ASHP) units and replacement rooftop solar photovoltaic (PV) array.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development shall be constructed strictly in accordance with the approved amended Energy Statement. Prior to the first occupation of the dwelling, 'as-built' SAP calculation outputs must be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority to verify that the targeted carbon dioxide emission reductions have been achieved in practice. The approved sustainable energy measures shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to the first occupation of the residential unit, a completed Water Efficiency Calculator for New Dwellings must be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The calculation shall demonstrate that maximum internal potable water usage will not exceed 110 litres per person per day, calculated using the national methodology under Part G of the Building Regulations.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 33 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to the commencement of works, a detailed Construction Logistics Plan (CLP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority in consultation with the Highways team. The plan must establish management measures for delivery routing, site access, vehicle tracking, loading and unloading, and the prevention of highway conflicts along Manor Road and the adjacent junction during construction operations.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 36 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and Policy T7 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "Prior to the first occupation of the residential unit hereby approved, detailed plans showing the provision of the dedicated additional cycle parking space within the existing site facilities shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved cycle parking space shall be fully provided before occupation and retained thereafter for cycle storage purposes.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 37 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and Policy T5 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Strategy prepared by Accord Architecture August 2025.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
  ],
